  "description": "Full Re sweep (20,40,100,200) of the circular-cylinder bounce-back method against benchmarks/cylinder.json's literature values, run right after fixing the N=3 bounce-back divergence (childOriginX/Y mis-registration in shaders/amr_manage_pool.wgsl + the L1->L2 force-refine coverage margin in main-cylinder-amr.js -- see that commit and main-cylinder-amr.js's own comment above N_LEVELS). Covers three configs at the same Re values: the dense (non-AMR) reference, AMR N_LEVELS=2, and AMR N_LEVELS=3, all with ?bounceback. All 12 (config x Re) cases pass. Produced by an ad hoc sweep script (tools/lib/cylinder-metrics.js's runCase driven directly, one CDP tab reused across all runs, same pattern as tools/validate-all.js) -- not a committed tool, just this one snapshot.",
